A||||6||Alex2004||My tach is jumping!||||4||
Z||000000||Alex2004||02-12-2001||08:02 PM||||Today i went outside to move the car in the garage, but i drove it to the house first, and when i got in, i seen that my tach was jumping around about every 10 seconds.  It goes to about to 2 1/2, 3 rpm but the engine doesn't seem to do anything but idle.  Does anyone know what is causing this?  Let me know, thanks...  Alex...<P> <A HREF="mailto:AbercrombieAlex15@hotmail.com">AbercrombieAlex15@hotmail.com</A> ||||reg||4
Z||000001||Old Lar||02-12-2001||08:26 PM||||Tach filter, loose connection somewhere.  My money is the tach filter.||||reg||3
Z||000002||c m west||02-12-2001||10:18 PM||||it is possible that the return curcuit from the tach filter is grounding out or that the tach filter itself is at fault - we can supply you with an upgrade to the standard tach filter if you are interested<P>Eric - West Coast Fiero||||reg||1
Z||000003||Alex2004||02-12-2001||11:06 PM||||Umm, what and where is the tach filter? Oh, i guess i also should have said it is an 84 SE.  This is the first time i had seen it jump like that, and when i started it earlier it didn't jump like earlier.  So let me know what, where, and how much a Tach filter cost's ok.  Thanks....<P>Alex...||||reg||5
Z||000004||filthyscarecrow||02-13-2001||01:13 AM||||replace your ignition wires. that solved the problem on mine. one wire was bad and caused it to jump. pull them off the cap and see if one of the poles is corroded. try replacing that wire before you screw with the tach filter. <P>------------------<BR>allow me to show you my exhaust pipes...||||reg||1
Z||000005||Larry Moss||02-13-2001||05:12 PM||||Alex:<P>I would take a quick look at the distributor itself.  The distributor shaft on the fiero is prone to rust, and this, by itself, can cause the tech to flux.  <P>I fixed my tach problem by using a fine grade of steel wool to rub clean all visibly rusted surfaces.  However, take caution and do not move the car or even rotate the distributor (because you can screw up the bottom timing).<P>A more effective cleaning may result with just a spray or two of wd40  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> or some mild de-rusting solution.<P><BR>  <A HREF="mailto:AbercrombieAlex15@hotmail.com">AbercrombieAlex15@hotmail.com</A>  [/B][/QUOTE]<P>||||reg||1
Z||000006||Alex2004||02-13-2001||08:15 PM||||Ok, thanks.  Something wierd though, the other day i got my rear defrost switch since it did not have one but does have defrost and the wires, and it does work.  But that is when i noticed that the tach was jumping, and when it starts moving, it doesn't move around much, but yesterday it was bizzurk, so does anyone know if that could be causeing it to do that?  Let me know, thanks...Alex<BR><p>[This message has been edited by Alex2004 (edited 02-13-2001).]||||reg||1
